In a Monday (Nov. 16) post, Cardi wrote, &#8220;A long a&#8211; week celebrating your birthday because it’s GREYS WORLD 🩶🩶🩶love you my fat man ..A TIME WAS HAD !!!&#8221;

The carousel featured a photo and video of the Grammy winner holding her son — who looks fly in a fuzzy Chanel hat &#8212; in a venue decked out with balloon sculptures, rocket ships, large recreations of the solar system&#8217;s planets and colorful lights. One clip finds Cardi and her youngest dancing around with a Transformers -esque anthropomorphic robot, and other photos show Grey&#8217;s lavish Mickey Mouse cake and food stands serving McDonalds, Popeyes, sushi, ice cream and more.

Cardi shares Grey with ex Stefon Diggs. Up until a couple of weeks ago, fans did not know what the little boy looked like, much less his name; the hip-hop star finally revealed both in an emotional Instagram post on Nov. 4. &#8220;It’s only been 1 year since meeting you but it feels like I’ve had you at my side forever,” she wrote at the time. “I carried you through one of the most uncertain high pressured times of my life but having you inside of me through it all gave me an extra strength . I was growing you inside of me and at the same time you were giving me life!&#8221;

The musician &#8212; whose Billboard 20 0 -topping LP Am I the Drama? just so happened to score a best rap album Grammy nomination on Monday &#8212; also shares three children with ex Offset. Daughters Kulture and Blossom and son Wave were seemingly all in attendance at baby brother Grey&#8217;s birthday extravaganza, posing together in another photo Cardi included in her post.
